  "default_clone_weights_note": "Rare pre-existing ESR1-mutant subclones. The research prior is 1e-5 to 1e-3 of cells (ASSUMPTION); a lattice of ~1500 cells cannot hold that, so the demo seeds 0.5% of each ESR1 mutant and no CDK escape, which arises by transition.",
  "drugs": [
    {
      "id": "endocrine",
      "label": "Endocrine suppression (aromatase inhibitor)",
      "exposure": "global",
      "mechanism": "estrogen_deprivation",
      "half_life_hours": 48.0,
      "reference_concentration_nm": 1.0,
      "units": "normalized estrogen deprivation (1.0 = maximal aromatase-inhibitor pressure, estrogen availability ~0.05)",
      "note": "Aromatase inhibitors act systemically, so this is a uniform environment level, not a diffusing tumour field."
    },
    {
      "id": "palbociclib",
      "label": "Palbociclib (CDK4/6 inhibitor)",
      "exposure": "diffusing",
      "mechanism": "CDK4_6_inhibitor",
      "half_life_hours": 29.0,
      "reference_concentration_nm": 1500.0,
      "reference_note": "Exposure 1.0 = 1500 nM at the vessel, twice the MCF-7 in-vitro IC50 (~70% effect on sensitive cells). ASSUMPTION: chosen so the sensitive clone is controlled at full exposure; clinical plasma levels (~100-130 nM at 125 mg) are not used directly because in-vitro and in-vivo scales differ. Half-life 29 h is the mean plasma elimination half-life (DIRECT, prescribing information)."
    },
    {
      "id": "fulvestrant",
      "label": "Fulvestrant (SERD)",
      "exposure": "diffusing",
      "mechanism": "estrogen_receptor_degrader",
      "half_life_hours": 960.0,
      "reference_concentration_nm": 25.0,
      "reference_note": "Exposure 1.0 = 25 nM, about the steady-state plasma level of 500 mg monthly dosing (DERIVED). Terminal half-life ~40 days (DIRECT, prescribing information)."
    },
    {
      "id": "elacestrant",
      "label": "Elacestrant (oral SERD)",
      "exposure": "diffusing",
      "mechanism": "estrogen_receptor_degrader",
      "half_life_hours": 40.0,
      "reference_concentration_nm": 150.0,
      "reference_note": "Exposure 1.0 = 150 nM at the vessel. ASSUMPTION: an oral SERD exposure several-fold above the parental IC50, which is what lets oral SERDs cover ESR1 mutants; not derived from pharmacokinetics and randomised over 50-300 nM. Half-life 30-50 h (DIRECT, prescribing information)."
    }
  ],
